{
  "dom_id": "step-q164248",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere $(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+(z+4)^{2}=5?$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-(-1))^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+(z-(-4))^{2}=(\\sqrt{5})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(-1,2,-4)$ and the radius $r=\\sqrt{5}.$",
